      "review_status": "approved_complete_component",
      "hypotheses": [
        "Genuine probability measure, a.e.-measurable real noise, a.e. bounded interval, true zero integral."
      ],
      "assessment": "The actual Hoeffding lemma derives the moment-generating-function bound with half-interval-width squared. The symmetric interval specializes to the actual R-sub-Gaussian convention. This is an unconditional component, not the conditional-past premise by itself.",
