        "SafeLearning.CompleteAppliedAzuma.bounded_centered_is_real_conditional_subgaussian"
      ],
      "review_status": "approved_complete_component",
      "hypotheses": [
        "Probability measure; conditioning sigma algebra m below the ambient measurable space; measurable actual noise; a.e. |noise|<=R with R nonnegative; its actual conditional expectation given m equals zero a.e.",
        "ConditionalBounds uses a Standard Borel ambient space. ConditionalLaw and Azuma remove that restriction by disintegrating the real-valued noise instead."
      ],
      "assessment": "The proofs construct the actual real conditional distribution, transport bounded support and zero conditional mean to that law, prove exponential integrability, then apply Hoeffding to obtain exp(lambda^2 R^2/2). The arbitrary-space formulation establishes the actual conditional-expectation inequality for every fixed real lambda. No independence or asserted desired MGF bound is substituted for the bounded-noise hypotheses.",
