      "hypotheses": [
        "A genuine filtration, every increment strongly measurable at its next filtration stage, and actual conditional sub-Gaussian increment laws at its current stage."
      ],
      "assessment": "Actual conditional-law composition identifies the joint law used in the MGF addition argument. Finite-prefix sums are adapted and their true MGF parameter n R^2 follows by induction; the past sum is measurable in the required sigma algebra. No independence between adapted increments is required.",
