      "assessment": "The genuine finite sum and conditional MGF induction yield actual event probability <=exp(-a^2/(2 T R^2)). The theorem retains the harmless totalized T=0 or R=0 cases; its bound there is 1. This scalar finite-horizon tail theorem supplies a real adapted-noise component and does not establish RKHS posterior concentration or an all-time self-normalized confidence event.",
